Great 🚀 — Day 44 – API Versioning & Backward Compatibility is what separates a mid-level developer from a senior backend engineer.

In real fintech systems, you CANNOT break existing clients (mobile apps, partners, payment gateways). That’s why versioning is critical.

1️⃣ Why Versioning is Required?
❌ Problem

You have API:

GET /accounts/{id}

Response:

{
  "id": 1,
  "balance": 1000
}

Now you change:

{
  "id": 1,
  "balance": 1000,
  "currency": "INR"
}

👉 Old clients may break ❌

2️⃣ What is Backward Compatibility?

👉 New changes should NOT break old clients

✔ Old apps continue working
✔ New apps use new features

3️⃣ API Versioning Strategies
🔹 1. URL Versioning (Most Common ✅)
/v1/accounts
/v2/accounts
Example
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/accounts")
public class AccountControllerV1 {
}
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v2/accounts")
public class AccountControllerV2 {
}

✔ Easy to understand
✔ Widely used in industry

🔹 2. Header Versioning
GET /accounts
Header: API-Version: v2
🔹 3. Query Param Versioning
/accounts?version=v2
🔹 4. Content Negotiation
Accept: application/vnd.bank.v2+json
